  "preText": "",
  "text": "<b>jaffa!</b> Leaps from a length and takes the glove through to Carey! Or does it...? Marais Erasmus and Crawley are unmoved, Australia perplexed. Cummins <b>reviews</b>, and this is going to be overturned. Clearly brushed the thumb on the bottom hand, Chris Gaffaney doesn't take long to overturn the decision. Boland has taken some unaccustomed punishment but nips in on the brink of lunch to give Australia a third wicket and some respite, as they walk off following their first skirmish with Bazball!",
  "postText": "<b>1.05pm:</b> Honours even? Advantage Australia? Who knows, in these hazy, crazy, Bazball-tinged days! Although, in some ways, you might say this contest has gone as expected - England threw their punches, scoring at close to 5 RPO, but Australia's attack showed their quality by prising out three important wickets. The dismissal of Zak Crawley, following a jaunty 61, will certainly lift the away dressing room (particularly after Australia failed to appeal when he apparently nicked behind on 40), but I think we can predict how England will approach things after lunch, when Harry Brook will join Joe Root on what looks a beautiful day for batting. Alex will be back for that in half an hour",
  "shortText": "Boland to Crawley, OUT",
